Rehomed here (2026-08-06): deferred ".." path-semantics alternative
---------------------------------------------------------------------
From cad-path-dotdot-resolution.issue (now CLOSED): clautolisp currently
does POSIX-UP for ".." on every platform and warns on any ".." outside
--lax (shipped 1.7.5). The probe matrix showed the native Windows CADs
(AutoCAD-Windows, BricsCAD-Windows) instead do syntactic-BACK, while
macOS BricsCAD and clautolisp everywhere do UP. A deferred alternative
was recorded but not scheduled: make clautolisp FOLLOW THE PLATFORM —
BACK on Windows, UP on Unix — so it matches whichever native CAD runs
beside it, at the cost of cross-OS clautolisp consistency. This is a
platform-dependent path-semantics choice on the same platform axis as the
"/..."-warns-on-autocad-windows case above, hence tracked here. Revisit if
the Windows divergence proves a problem in practice; not scheduled now.


Decision (pjb, 2026-10-03)
--------------------------
"we only have 2022 to test; more recent versions we only have the web
reference, so for now, let's say 2022 is the last known." So: NO bump to
2027 -- nothing newer than what we can test is declared characterised.

Open point raised back to pjb the same day, before changing anything:
*autolisp-dialect-latest-version* is (:autocad . 2026) today, and taking
it to 2022 is not one constant. Bare --dialect autocad is an ENUMERATED
alias of the :autocad-2026 descriptor (UTF-8 source default) and does not
read the constant; only DERIVED spellings do (autocad-mac, ...), and a
derived version < 2025 switches them to the ISO-8859-1 source default
(dialect.lisp %synthesize-dialect). Lowering only the constant would make
`autocad' and `autocad-mac' disagree. Choices: (a) record 2022 as the
last TESTED release and keep 2026 as the behavioural template (the 2026
web reference is what the catalogue was built from); or (b) make 2022 the
latest known everywhere, bare `autocad' included -- a behaviour change
(single-byte source default under --dialect autocad).

DECIDED (pjb, 2026-10-03): option (a). 2022 is recorded as the last TESTED
AutoCAD; 2026 stays the behavioural template and the value of
*autolisp-dialect-latest-version* (docstring updated). And a standing rule:
"when we have definite reference material specifying differences between
versions, we must implement them in different dialect versions, even if we
can't test them (yet). Possibly, we may write probes, and hope users will
contribute later probe results on their versions." Recorded in AGENTS.md,
"Dialect versions and products". Remaining work of this ticket is therefore
concrete: harvest the documented version differences (doc scans) into the
feature/version matrix and implement each behind the version facet, with a
probe per difference.


Documented version differences: harvested and first implemented (2026-10-04, clautolisp 2.2.173)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Doc scan (Autodesk "What's New or Changed with AutoLISP",
help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/<year>/ENU/AutoCAD-AutoLISP/files/GUID-037BF4D4-755E-4A5C-8136-80E85CCEDF3E.htm,
"About AutoLISP Compatibility" GUID-31FD1A96...; BricsCAD release notes
boa.bricscad.octave.com/common/releasenotes.jsp and the DevRef history
pages V11-V22.htm). The documented differences, by release:

AutoCAD: 2013 vlax-machine-product-key (vlax-product-key obsolete) / 2014
findtrustedfile, showHTMLModalWindow, SECURELOAD + TRUSTEDPATHS +
TRUSTEDDOMAINS + LEGACYCODESEARCH, findfile searches trusted paths / 2016
osnap "qui" invalid -> nil; getcfg / setcfg obsolete; signed LSP/FAS/VLX /
2017 CDATE / DATE / TD* no longer to the millisecond; EPDFSHX -> PDFSHX /
2019 LOCALE ISO-639 ("en" in the doc; measured "FR" on 2022) instead of
"ENU" / 2020 INSERT -> Blocks palette / 2021 LISPSYS (initial 1; 0 = MBCS VL
IDE, 1 = Unicode VS Code, 2 = Unicode, MBCS FAS); Unicode LSP sources;
(open f mode ["utf8"|"utf8-bom"]); Unicode semantics of ascii / chr /
strlen / substr / read-char / vl-string-* / vl-list->string etc. under
LISPSYS 1 / 2024 LT gets AutoLISP (no vlax-create-object & co.) / 2025
acet-load-expresstools / 2015, 2017-2020, 2022, 2026, 2027: no new or
changed functions. Mac: no ActiveX (vla- / vlax- / vlr- absent); the vl-
string / file functions present since 2011.
BricsCAD: V17 (open f "r,ccs=UTF-8|UTF-16LE|UNICODE") / V18.1 Unicode
ascii / chr, (ver) "10.0", tiny doubles print "0.0", dos_command / V19.1
(load "x.vlx"/"x.fas") as (load "x") / V19.2 vle-enableserverbusy / V20.1
UTF-8 / UTF-16LE LSP with BOM, vle-vector-*, (div) removed / V21.1 property
functions, vl-infp / vl-nanp, grvecs in DCS / V22 vla-PostCommand,
vle-file-encoding, (vl-cmdf) returns T / nil / V23.1 LISPSYS (BOM-less
UTF-8), vl-subent-*, vle-sunid / V24 vl-local-undo-*, UTF-8 DCL,
vle-file->list UTF-8, findfile nil on trailing spaces / V25.1 menu-macro
LISP always evaluated, vle-vector-to2d, LISPINIT=0 only with SDI=1 / V26.1
(mod) and (round) REMOVED; 26.2 chars > 255 written as \U+nnnn to ANSI
files.

IMPLEMENTED in 2.2.173:
  - autolisp-runtime/source/operator-versions.lisp: *VERSION-GATED-OPERATORS*
    (19 rows, sources cited) and the `[version-operator]' notice (registered
    tag; annex regenerated): a gated operator called under a dialect of its
    product whose version lacks it warns, once per operator; :error mode
    errors; versionless dialects never warn. E.g. acet-load-expresstools
    under autocad-2022; mod / round under bricscad-v26. The nil stubs are
    gated too.
  - Feature matrix rows :lispsys (AutoCAD 2021+, BricsCAD 23+; GETVAR
    "LISPSYS" -> nil before) and :locale-form (AutoCAD 2019+ upper-case
    language "FR", measured; BricsCAD "fr_FR"). BricsCAD's LISPSYS default
    0 (both harvests).
  - probes/sources/probe-versions.lsp: the gated operators' presence,
    LISPSYS, LOCALE, (ver) -- for AutoCAD 2022 / BricsCAD V26 now, and for
    users of other versions to contribute.

LEFT (larger, each its own slice):
  - The 2021 Unicode string semantics (ascii / chr / strlen / substr /
    vl-string-* ...) under LISPSYS 0 vs 1, and AutoCAD < 2021 behaving as
    LISPSYS 0 (MBCS).
  - OPEN's third argument "utf8" / "utf8-bom" (AutoCAD 2021+) vs BricsCAD's
    "r,ccs=UTF-8" mode spelling.
  - osnap "qui" -> nil from 2016; (vl-cmdf) -> T / nil from BricsCAD V22.2;
    BricsCAD V18.1 tiny-double printing; LOCALE's pre-2019 three-letter form
    (needs the code table measured).
  - QUESTION FOR PJB, not changed: *autolisp-feature-matrix* says AutoLISP
    source became UTF-8 by default in AutoCAD 2025 (:default-utf8-encoding,
    citing autolisp-spec ch.7). The Autodesk 2021 pages say LISPSYS (initial
    value 1 = Unicode) and Unicode LSP sources arrived in 2021. Moving the
    boundary to 2021 would change the source default of the autocad-2021 ..
    -2024 dialects -- an encoding-consolidation decision.

Measured (2026-10-04, probe-versions, AutoCAD 2022 job 16921684058, BricsCAD
V26 job 16921684059): acet-load-expresstools ABSENT on AutoCAD 2022 (the
2025 gate holds); mod / round ABSENT on BricsCAD V26 (the removal holds);
LOCALE "FR" / "fr_FR"; BricsCAD LISPSYS 0. NOTE: AutoCAD 2022 reports LISPSYS
0 on the CI machine where the doc says the initial value is 1 -- one machine
(its registry may carry a changed value) against the documentation, so the
autocad dialects keep 1; a second AutoCAD machine would settle it.
showhtmlmodalwindow is absent from AutoCAD 2022's CONSOLE (accoreconsole has
no UI) -- not a contradiction of the 2014 gate. vl-infp / vl-nanp exist on
AutoCAD 2022: filed as vl-infp-vl-nanp-exist-on-autocad.
ANSWERED (pjb 2026-10-04): "the default source encoding depends on LISPSYS.
Indeed, a new autocad installation will have LISPSYS=1; the users typically
set it [to 0] when they have windows-1252 code bases. ... We can align to
autocad, but we must read back the LISPSYS setting from persistent memory
(the registry)." Done in 2.2.175: the spec's encoding rule is "LISPSYS
decides, from 2021" (the forum-sourced 2025 note superseded); LISPSYS is
persisted per product in the host registry store and read at launch; the
AutoCAD dialects derive the source / file default from it, ahead of the
locale (end-to-end on the executable: a cp1252 file decodes under LISPSYS 0,
fails as UTF-8 under 1). The :default-utf8-encoding matrix row (unused by
the runtime) is left for the encoding-consolidation cleanup.


Remainder measured and implemented (2026-10-04, clautolisp 2.2.181)
-------------------------------------------------------------------

probe-triage2 (AutoCAD 2022 Windows job 16923993438, BricsCAD V26 Windows
16923993442 and macOS 16923993439), all at LISPSYS 0:

| form                                | AutoCAD 2022 | BricsCAD V26 Win | BricsCAD V26 macOS |
|-------------------------------------+--------------+------------------+--------------------|
| (ascii (chr 128))                   | 128          | 128              | 128                |
| (ascii (chr 8364))                  | 172          | 128              | 8364               |
| (strlen (chr 8364))                 | 1            | 1                | 1                  |
| (vl-string->list (chr 8364))        | (172)        | (128)            | (8364)             |
| (osnap p "_end") / "_qui,_end"      | nil / nil    | same point twice | nil / nil          |
| (vl-cmdf "_.LINE" ... "")           | T            | T                | T                  |
| (open f "w" "utf8")                 | ERROR "too many arguments" | FILE | FILE          |

DONE:
  - The 2021 Unicode string semantics: %character-code-mode -- :byte
    (AutoCAD Windows, before 2021 or LISPSYS 0: a code reduced to a
    windows-1252 byte), :cp1252 (BricsCAD Windows, LISPSYS 0), else
    Unicode -- for chr / ascii / vl-string->list / vl-list->string /
    vl-string-elt / vl-string-position / read-char / write-char.
  - OPEN's third argument: refused (wrong number of arguments) under
    AutoCAD before 2021 or the :byte mode; BricsCAD takes it.
  - (vl-cmdf) -> nil under BricsCAD dialects before V22 (release notes);
    T otherwise (measured on both).
  - osnap "qui": BricsCAD measured to ignore it; AutoCAD headless cannot
    tell (nil for every mode); clautolisp's osnap is a nil stub -- the
    documented AutoCAD 2016 rule ("qui" -> nil) holds trivially.
  - By the way: the LISPSYS foreign-dialect warning no longer fires under
    the BricsCAD dialects (BricsCAD has LISPSYS from V23, measured 0).
  Spec: *** Measured + *** clautolisp in ASCII, CHR, VL-STRING->LIST,
  OPEN, VL-CMDF, OSNAP.

LEFT: BricsCAD V18.1 tiny-double printing; LOCALE's pre-2019 three-letter
form (needs the code table measured); AutoCAD at LISPSYS 1 measured (the CI
machine is at 0) -- the Unicode side is documented, not measured.
